==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Sea Mistress Ruri''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Mer-Queen Ruri''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Sea Maiden Ruri is a surprisingly underwhelming unit. Despite being able to achieve massive health over [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemies, [[Single Attack]] gets in the way of her severely. Her [[Multi-Hit]] can partially relieve this issue, but then her range comes in. All three combined usually end up making her hit a unit on one hit, but not the others, drastically lowering her great DPS.

Use her primarily for tanky Red enemies like [[Bore]], better if they lack knockbacks. Her [[Weaken|weaken]] uptime is surprisingly good, lasting for 5 seconds and 6.67 seconds in her [[True Form]]. Her Multi-Hit increases her weaken chance too. Additionally, her combo enhances the resistant ability, further increasing her effective HP if you use her correctly.

For generalist usage, it's best not to bother. Only use her for a bit of extra padding in stages where you have no better alternatives.

==='''True Form'''===
Mer-Queen Ruri gets significantly expanded DPS and health, and that's pretty much it. Nothing is solved, she can just make up for her weaknesses better. Her DPS is even better than before, but Single Target and Multi-Hit bring it down massively as always. Against singular bosses, she's even better than ever, but that's still the only place you'll be able to use her to her full potential.

==='''Talents'''===
The basic stat boosts can help make her already great stats even better, though you'd need some [[Catseye]] investment beforehand.

[[Special Abilities#Resist|Slow Resist]] allows Ruri to not get affected as much by the few slowing enemies she may run into (the only relevant target is [[Professor A.]]), but it doesn't help her all that much.

Relic targeting and Curse Immunity gives her usage in [[Uncanny Legends]] against the various relics encountered, putting her abilities to good use as Relics are notorious for having several nasty threats that are difficult to approach, namely [[Othom]]. Hilariously, she serves as a great wall against [[Zero Luza]], of all enemies once both Curse Immunity and Target Relic are unlocked, since her weaken helps massively once Zero Luza is strengthened.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
Mer-Queen Ruri's '''Dodge''' talent is without question the best Ultra Talent she gets. Relic and Red enemies have a good number of enemies that attack rather quickly. Combined with her 2 second dodge duration per activation, and she will be dodging a lot of attacks. This fact is stressed out even more since she has Resistant to and Weaken against both traits, making her both able to dodge frequently as well as being very tanky even without the dodge.

'''Immune to Freeze''' isn't particularly useful since there are only two Red enemies and two Relic enemies in the game that utilize Freeze, but it makes her better in stages that mix in other enemies capable of Freeze, such as [[Henry]].

'''Movement Speed Up''' is also not particularly useful since she is meant to be a mid-ranged tank, and hence, movement speed isn't particularly useful if she isn't going to be directly in the enemies face. At best, she can now get to the battlefield a good bit faster, which isn't worth the NP at that point.

